.TH XFWM4 1 "October 2026" "xfwm4-gl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xfwm4 \- Xfce window manager with OpenGL compositing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xfwm4
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
xfwm4-gl replaces the Xfce window manager while retaining the xfwm4 command,
themes and xfconf settings. OpenGL compositing is enabled by default, with
automatic XRender fallback when accelerated rendering is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --replace
Replace the running window manager.
.TP
.BR --compositor= on|off|auto
Select the compositor mode.
.TP
.BR --vblank= auto|adaptive|off|glx|xpresent
Select synchronization behavior at startup.
.TP
.B --help
Show available command-line options.
.TP
.B --version
Show the version and compiled features.
.SH SETTINGS
The xfwm4 xfconf channel retains the original window manager settings.
The /general/use_gl_compositing setting enables OpenGL rendering.
The /general/suspend_compositing_fullscreen setting controls compositor
suspension for focused fullscreen windows.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XFWM4_GL_BACKEND=glx
Request GLX instead of the default EGL backend.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Use xprop -root _XFWM4_RENDER_BACKEND _XFWM4_VSYNC to inspect the active renderer.
.SH SEE ALSO
xfconf-query(1)
.PP
https://github.com/fulalas/xfwm4-gl
